   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch2/q1",
   "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{1-2x}\\right),\\qquad|x|&lt;\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm d^2y}{\\mathrm dx^2}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm d^3y}{\\mathrm dx^3}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence, or otherwise, find the series expansion of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{1}{1-2x}\\right)\"></span> about <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\"></span>, in ascending powers of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>, up to and including the term in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3\"></span>. Give each coefficient in its simplest form. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Use your expansion to find an approximate value for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln\\left(\\dfrac32\\right)\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
