   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch2/q2",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Use the standard summation formulae to show that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}(3r^2-17r-25)=n(n^2-An-B)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are integers to be determined.</p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li><p>Explain why, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\in\\mathbb N\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{3k}r\\tan(60r)^\\circ=-k\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Using the results from part (a) and part (b) and showing all your working,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li><p>determine any value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> that satisfies</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=5}^{n}(3r^2-17r-25)=15\\left[\\sum_{r=6}^{3n}r\\tan(60r)^\\circ\\right]^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
