   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch2/q9",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Show that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{1}{r^2}-\\frac{1}{(r+1)^2}\\equiv\\frac{2r+1}{r^2(r+1)^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li><p>Hence prove that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}\\frac{2r+1}{r^2(r+1)^2}=\\frac{n(n+2)}{(n+1)^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><p>Show that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n&gt;1\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=n}^{3n}\\frac{6r+3}{r^2(r+1)^2}=\\frac{an^2+bn+c}{n^2(3n+1)^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
