   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch2/q11",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Show that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r-3+\\frac{1}{r+1}-\\frac{1}{r+2}=\\frac{r^3-7r-5}{(r+1)(r+2)}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li><p>Hence prove, using the method of differences, that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}\\frac{r^3-7r-5}{(r+1)(r+2)}=\\frac{n(n^2+an+b)}{2(n+2)}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
